// W5-24 U3a/t, S-600, R3 (spec §18.1: "`@` の属性の修正候補は、その属性を可視性と `rt` の前（既にある属性の後ろ）へ移す形である（属性の中身の誤りは移した後の検査で報告し、中身が読めなければ候補を作らない）";
// "候補が写すか動かす部分（移す属性）に同じ段の別の誤りがあっても、形そのものが読めれば候補を出し、残りの誤りは当てた後の検査で報告する"): an attribute after `pub` that is read as a form but has
// an error of its own (an attribute that the table does not have, a value out of the list, a value of `@repr` out of the list, the
// old `@derive(Eq)` and the old `@relaxed`) has the one candidate that moves it, and what is wrong inside it is reported after the
// move (`leaves`: the position in the fixed text, the attribute at the first column; the E0005 of the unknown attribute and of the
// value, the E0020 of the old forms). One error in each declaration unit (P-01).

@nope pub fn bad_name(x: F32) -> F32 {              //~ E0002
  x
}

@fp(fast) pub fn bad_value(x: F32) -> F32 {         //~ E0002
  x
}

@repr(rust) pub struct BadRepr {                    //~ E0002
  x: I32,
}

@derive(Eq) pub struct BadDerive {                  //~ E0002
  x: I32,
}

@relaxed pub fn bad_old(x: F32) -> F32 {            //~ E0002
  x
}
